    {
      "name": "meta",
      "value": {
        "title": "pij skill realignment: findings ledger, rulings, two-sided verb gate",
        "plan": "../plan.dd.json#meta",
        "version": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "architecture",
      "value": {
        "principles": "The code and --help are the authority; docs/how is second; the skill is the thing being corrected. Work file by file with the survey row open, re-verify each finding before acting (the survey can be wrong: REJECTED is a valid disposition with proof), and record the disposition in assets/findings.md as you go. Cite, don't restate: where docs/how or a convention (C1-C12) already holds the rule, link it. A finding that exposes a code bug becomes a pij-fleet issue, not a code change. The two gates read the authorities directly (RS_ROUTE_TABLE; the built pij-rs --help) and never copy a verb list (consume the producer, not a duplicate).",
        "composition_root": "skills/pij/SKILL.md (registry, verb coverage, invariants) with references/00-routing.md conventions; the route and prime files cite them",
        "contracts": [
          "assets/findings.md: one row per survey row: report, line, verdict, disposition (FIXED|RULED|REJECTED|DEFERRED), evidence",
          "SKILL.md coverage: shim verbs in the existing table (parsed by the TS test); native-only pij-rs subcommands in a separate table the TS forward check does not parse",
          "crates/cli/tests/skill_verb_coverage.rs: parse `pij-rs --help` subcommands, assert each appears in SKILL.md"
        ],
        "seams": [
          ".omp/extensions/pij/core/generation-skill-coverage.test.ts (skillVerbs parser stops at the next '## ' heading)",
          ".omp/extensions/pij/core/generation-routing.ts RS_ROUTE_TABLE",
          "crates/cli/src/main.rs clap subcommands (binary pij-rs)"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "fan_out",
      "value": {
        "decision": "solo-pm",
        "rationale": "One coherent text with cross-file consistency ACs (AC7); splitting by file would recreate the contradictions this plan removes. One coder implements; a cross-family reviewer re-surveys; the prime verifies and merges."
      }
    },
